"{\"blocks\":[{\"k\":\"t\",\"v\":\"I’d choose the Aeroplan award departing late on January 15: among the award choices shown, it has the shortest elapsed time and requires fewer points than the other two. The tradeoff is a later Bangkok arrival than either alternative. All three selected awards are one-stop economy itineraries; the results do not specify the cabin of each individual flight.\"},{\"k\":\"p\",\"r\":\"J14@2027-01-15T23:15-08:00/SFO>BKK/E>2027-01-17T09:50\",\"n\":\"Best balance: late departure, shorter journey\",\"v\":\"Departs SFO at 11:15 p.m. January 15 and arrives in Bangkok at 9:50 a.m. January 17 local time. This Aeroplan award is 65,000 points plus CAD 107.40 in quoted fees (quote scope is unknown). It has one stop in Hong Kong, with a reported 70-minute connection, and nine seats shown. Its 19h 35m elapsed time is 2h 50m shorter than the January 15 midday option and 5h 15m shorter than the other afternoon option. Downside: it arrives later than both alternatives. The reported economy cabin does not establish the cabin on each leg.\"},{\"k\":\"x\",\"r\":\"T06\"},{\"k\":\"x\",\"r\":\"T09\"},{\"k\":\"a\",\"r\":\"J7@2027-01-15T12:00-08:00/SFO>BKK/E>2027-01-17T01:25\",\"n\":\"Earlier arrival: midday departure\",\"v\":\"Departs SFO at noon January 15 and arrives in Bangkok at 1:25 a.m. January 17 local time—5h 5m earlier than the recommended option. This Aeroplan award costs 65,000 points plus CAD 116.50 in quoted fees (scope unknown), with one stop in Taipei and a reported 4h 30m connection. One seat is shown. At 22h 25m, it takes 2h 50m longer than the recommendation. Consider it if the earlier arrival matters more than the longer journey and higher quoted fees.\"},{\"k\":\"x\",\"r\":\"T05\"},{\"k\":\"a\",\"r\":\"J12@2027-01-15T14:40-08:00/SFO>BKK/E>2027-01-17T06:30\",\"n\":\"Lower quoted fees: afternoon departure\",\"v\":\"Departs SFO at 2:40 p.m. January 15 and arrives in Bangkok at 6:30 a.m. January 17 local time. This Aeroplan award is 92,144 points plus CAD 43.90 in quoted fees (scope unknown), with one stop in Vancouver and a reported 6h 15m connection. Nine seats are shown. Its 24h 50m elapsed time is the longest of these three options, and it uses more Aeroplan points than either alternative. Choose it if its lower quoted fee is more important to you than the extra points and longer trip.\"},{\"k\":\"b\",\"r\":\"C4@2027-01-15T12:00-08:00/SFO>BKK\",\"n\":\"Cash baseline: EVA Air\",\"v\":\"The selected cash itinerary departs SFO at noon January 15 and arrives in Bangkok at 11:40 p.m. January 16 local time. It is a one-stop itinerary via Taipei, takes 20h 40m, and is quoted at USD 525. The price scope is unknown, so this is a separate cash reference—not a confirmed per-person or party total, and not directly comparable to an award’s points-plus-fees cost.\"},{\"k\":\"t\",\"v\":\"The award fee quotes are in CAD and their scope is unknown; do not assume they are per traveler or all-in totals. Seat counts and prices may change, so confirm current availability and booking terms with the provider. These are selected examples from search results, not the full eligible inventory; search coverage was partial. Check the exact connection and ticketing details before booking—an airport connection alone does not establish ticket protection.\"}]}"
